1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,420
Tonight, the moon disappears.

2
00:00:02,920 --> 00:00:05,060
No explosion, no warning.

3
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:07,680
One moment it's there, the next,

4
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:08,720
it's gone.

5
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:10,680
People rush outside.

6
00:00:10,960 --> 00:00:12,700
Scientists search the sky.

7
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:15,880
But the real danger isn't happening above us.

8
00:00:15,960 --> 00:00:17,720
It's beginning down here.

9
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:20,860
10 days later, on a beach in California,

10
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:24,200
thousands of tiny fish are waiting to be born.

11
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:26,320
They're buried beneath the sand.

12
00:00:26,620 --> 00:00:29,340
Normally, the next series of high tides washes

13
00:00:29,380 --> 00:00:31,840
over their eggs and triggers them to hatch.

14
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:34,680
But without the moon, the tides are weaker and

15
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:36,300
their patterns have changed.

16
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:38,800
Some eggs might never be reached by the water

17
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:42,240
in time. A generation of fish could die before

18
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:44,020
ever entering the ocean.

19
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:45,860
And that's just the beginning.

20
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:49,760
Across tropical reefs, corals face another problem.

21
00:00:50,060 --> 00:00:52,500
Many depend on lunar cycles to release their

22
00:00:52,540 --> 00:00:54,960
reproductive cells at the same time.

23
00:00:55,120 --> 00:00:57,420
Without those signals, their timing could fall

24
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:00,320
apart. Fewer eggs are fertilized.

25
00:01:00,460 --> 00:01:02,400
Fewer young corals survive.

26
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:05,240
And over the years, struggling reefs could leave

27
00:01:05,280 --> 00:01:07,540
fish with fewer places to live.

28
00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:10,100
Now imagine the fishermen who depend on those

29
00:01:10,140 --> 00:01:11,060
ecosystems.

30
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:13,940
Fewer fish could mean empty nets,

31
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:16,940
lost income, and entire coastal communities

32
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:18,460
forced to adapt.

33
00:01:18,840 --> 00:01:21,780
Even on land, the darkness changes things.

34
00:01:21,980 --> 00:01:24,500
Some nighttime predators gain an advantage.

35
00:01:24,720 --> 00:01:26,960
Other animals lose the moonlight they relied

36
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,560
on to spot danger.

37
00:01:28,880 --> 00:01:31,600
And far into the future, Earth's seasons could

38
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:34,260
become less predictable as its axis behaves

39
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:35,120
differently.

40
00:01:35,460 --> 00:01:36,820
The terrifying part?

41
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:39,940
Humanity might survive the moon's disappearance,

42
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:42,800
but some species could struggle to reproduce

43
00:01:42,900 --> 00:01:46,420
and some future generations might never be born.

44
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:49,000
The moon wasn't just lighting our nights.

45
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:51,920
It was helping keep parts of life on Earth in

46
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:52,580
rhythm.

47
00:01:53,360 --> 00:01:56,300
What if… The Unknown File

